{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"f34414621e164e4c08b7248f1bb96655b5dbc2567205a6ae232e9349e4b7af28","digest":{"component_or_area":"GitHub Actions workflow gates","key_entities":[".github/workflows/test.yml","gerrit-verify.yaml","scripts/check_readme_quickstart.py","scripts/probe_rebar.py","tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py","test_completeness_every_gate_step_is_guarded_or_marked","test_empty_tree_every_guarded_step_skips_cleanly","test_golden_path_guards_match_the_verified_lane"],"problem_keywords":["predates-gate guard","workflow script guard","golden-path gate","test.yml","mirror lane parity"],"propositions":["The golden-path job in test.yml runs check_readme_quickstart.py and probe_rebar.py without predates-gate guards, causing false red failures when the change predates the script.","The Verified lane in gerrit-verify.yaml guards the same two scripts with canonical [ ! -f <path> ] guards and skip messages, but test.yml lacks this parity.","Both golden-path steps must carry -f guards naming their scripts with the canonical skip message to prevent redding the mirror lane on gate faults.","The predates-gate guard parity test suite must verify that every step running either script in either lane carries its own guard and canonical message."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787612939673474001,"uuid":"cbb3586e-cff2-4a51-b459-9e15d11d153a"}